From 519ad9dfda67f853c5f3839f1d83e53b009e70c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: focus1 <focus1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:22:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: guard the null product global in advanced product labels

Restores the guard reverted in #1516, moved to sit immediately after
`global $product;` instead of further down.

Position matters: composer-patches applies patches through the
web/app/plugins symlink into local-plugins, so the committed source
carries the change and the patch is expected to fail as already-applied
on every install. With the guard lower in the method its leading context
(`return;` / `}` / blank) also matched the end of the inserted block, so
patch found a second valid anchor and duplicated it (#1516). Anchored to
`global $product;` the context is unique and occurs once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 class-wapl-global-labels.php | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/class-wapl-global-labels.php b/class-wapl-global-labels.php
index 46c715536..76d6707d3 100644
--- a/class-wapl-global-labels.php
+++ b/class-wapl-global-labels.php
@@ -45,6 +45,11 @@ class WAPL_Global_Labels {
 		/** @var $product WC_Product */
 		global $product;
 
+		// Templates may fire the hook outside the product loop, leaving $product unset.
+		if ( ! $product instanceof \WC_Product ) {
+			return;
+		}
+
 		// Stop if global labels are disabled
 		if ( 'no' == get_option( 'enable_wapl', 'yes' ) ) {
 			return;
-- 
